# UI/UX workflow

Entry: `DESIGN.md` → task-specific docs in `docs/design/`, `docs/ux/`, `docs/product/`.

## Before changing UI

1. Read `DESIGN.md` (brand, do/don't)
2. Read relevant flow in `docs/ux/flows/`
3. Read `docs/design/FOUNDATIONS.md` + `COMPONENT_STANDARDS.md`
4. Inspect `src/components/ui/` and `/dev/ui` UI Lab
5. List all states: loading, empty, error, success, disabled
6. Propose plan — do not redesign unrelated screens

## Design requirements

- Use semantic tokens from `globals.css` `@theme` — no arbitrary values
- Reuse `src/components/ui/` components (`Button`, `Card`, `Dialog`, etc.)
- One primary (accent) CTA per view
- Vietnamese UI copy; hanzi is visual hero on learning screens
- Mobile + desktop behavior intentional
- Support `prefers-reduced-motion`
- All states designed — not just happy path

## Engineering requirements

- Preserve business logic and API contracts
- No new UI dependencies without justification
- Semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, visible focus
- Run `npm run quality` before finishing

## Agent roles (multi-turn)

1. Auditor — read only, no code changes
2. Implementer — follow specs, no new visual direction
3. QA Reviewer — compare code vs `docs/qa/VISUAL_QA.md`

## Golden slice reference

Practice + SRS + Inferno + Dashboard — complete these to ≥80 scorecard before scaling.
